<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sambre</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sambre is a river of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, flowing about 190 km north-east to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> at Namur. It is usually identified with the Sabis of Caesar's account, where the Nervii were defeated in 57 BCE. It later flowed through the counties of Hainaut and Namur and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> region of Charleroi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sambre.jpg" alt="Sambre" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Pol GRANDMONT · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Namur_JPG02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
